  "evidence": [
    {
      "id": "E1",
      "source": "ORG-01",
      "quote": "Org chart v3 (January 2026): Maintenance Operations sits over Planning, Base, Line and Stores. Quality and Safety, Technical Services, Finance, IT, HR, Customer Programmes and the Programme Office report to the Executive Committee.",
      "speaker": "",
      "attribution": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "E2",
      "source": "INT-01",
      "quote": "My planners ring Stores before they raise anything. If Stores say it's not on the shelf we plan around it.",
      "speaker": "Head of Planning",
      "attribution": "testimony"
    },
    {
      "id": "E3",
      "source": "INT-01",
      "quote": "Engineers sign off at the end and they hold the release. When Raj says the card's not ready, the hangar waits, no matter what my schedule says.",
      "speaker": "Head of Planning",
      "attribution": "testimony"
    },
    {
      "id": "E4",
      "source": "INT-01",
      "quote": "Night shift re-sequences the cards themselves. By the time the plan reaches them it's already wrong. I find out in the morning.",
      "speaker": "Head of Planning",
      "attribution": "testimony"
    },
    {
      "id": "E5",
      "source": "INT-01",
      "quote": "I want the system. I don't want to be the team that loses a week of planning to it during cutover.",
      "speaker": "Head of Planning",
      "attribution": "testimony"
    },
    {
      "id": "E6",
      "source": "INT-02",
      "quote": "Before any procedure change goes to CAAS I talk to Raj. If Raj says the engineers won't accept it, I don't send it.",
      "speaker": "Quality Manager",
      "attribution": "testimony"
    },
    {
      "id": "E7",
      "source": "INT-02",
      "quote": "I speak to our CAAS inspector informally before a submission. It saves three rounds.",
      "speaker": "Quality Manager",
      "attribution": "testimony"
    },
    {
      "id": "E8",
      "source": "INT-02",
      "quote": "Any new maintenance record system has to keep the audit trail. If it doesn't, I will not sign.",
      "speaker": "Quality Manager",
      "attribution": "testimony"
    },
    {
      "id": "E9",
      "source": "INT-02",
      "quote": "I heard Finance is sitting on the purchase orders for the cutover contractors.",
      "speaker": "Quality Manager",
      "attribution": "hearsay"
    },
    {
      "id": "E10",
      "source": "INT-03",
      "quote": "The plan comes at six and by midnight it is wrong. We re-sequence the cards ourselves and tell Planning in the morning.",
      "speaker": "Night shift supervisor",
      "attribution": "testimony"
    },
    {
      "id": "E11",
      "source": "INT-03",
      "quote": "The technicians do what I tell them. If I say the new tablet is fine, they use it. If I say it's rubbish, it's in a drawer by Friday.",
      "speaker": "Night shift supervisor",
      "attribution": "testimony"
    },
    {
      "id": "E12",
      "source": "INT-03",
      "quote": "Everybody asks Raj. He signs the release, so what he thinks is what happens.",
      "speaker": "Night shift supervisor",
      "attribution": "testimony"
    },
    {
      "id": "E13",
      "source": "INT-03",
      "quote": "The union rep sits in the canteen at shift change. Whatever is said there is the shift's view by morning. That is what I have seen, I could not tell you how he gets it.",
